{"seq":27,"id":"AC3.CK1","type":"check","at":"2026-10-30T14:09:18Z","by":"AC3","prev":"sha256:fdd477477910231b0372fdcc8b885b9991ca29c07c0f97999678c7b612e8fdf3","content_hash":"sha256:346506e3f03b4e7a232a2010440a86fe5fd36b2b3ef3b6bd48ff8d23d7942b40","supersedes":null,"origin":null,"body":{"target":"H5","outcome":"confirmed","extent":"full","notes":"Re-derived C9 from D3 by my own enumeration over o in {0,1} at x=p (AC3.RN1, results AC3.RS1-RS6; own code, study code not used). Sympy: E[1+e_a]=2-p+(1-p)^2/(1+p) and E[1+e_b]=1+p+p^2/(2-p) reduce to zero difference; E[1+e_a]-1=2(1-p)/(1+p)>0 and E[1+e_b]-1=2p/(2-p)>0 for all p in (0,1) (analytic, positive factors). Additive: E log(1+e_a)=g(p)=p log((2-p)/p)+(1-p)log((1-p)/(1+p)), E log(1+e_b)=-g, g(1-p)=-g(p), g(1/2)=0 (sympy). Sign of g proved analytically by my own route: g=2p atanh(1-p)-2(1-p)atanh(p)=2p(1-p)[phi(1-p)-phi(p)] with phi(t)=atanh(t)/t strictly increasing (power series with positive coefficients), so g>0 for p<1/2, <0 for p>1/2. Also checked at 50 digits on 22,024 points (grid, fine grid, p down to 1e-40 and up to 1-1e-40): 0 unreduced identities, 0 counterexamples (AC3.RS1, RS2). No disagreement with derivations.md section 2."}}
{"seq":28,"id":"AC3.CK2","type":"check","at":"2026-10-30T14:09:22Z","by":"AC3","prev":"sha256:4e0bae00cab5569b975da5a8e9c26aeaa1dc85a7947d1d5c2365b98ced7d079e","content_hash":"sha256:967a00b0b2129070f7052f062d1a701d5f7b5652587e2c253aa45d19e348af49","supersedes":null,"origin":null,"body":{"target":"H6","outcome":"disputed","extent":"full","notes":"Everything checked holds except one wording point. AC3.RN2 (results AC3.RS7-RS12; own code): multiplicative case from D3/D9 by enumeration: h_b=-2(x^2-2x+p)/((2-x)(1-x)) and h_a=2(p-x^2)/(x(1+x)) (sympy), only root in (0,1) is 1-sqrt(1-p) resp. sqrt(p); with q=sqrt(1-p), p-x*=q(1-q)>0 and sqrt(p)-p=s(1-s)>0; h factorises with sign of (x-x*) (iETS_I) and (x*-x) (iETS_O), so unique and stable. Additive case, my own proof: h_b=2atanh(x)[(1-p)-pR(x)], R=atanh(1-x)/atanh(x) strictly decreasing from +inf to 0, so a unique root with R(x*)=(1-p)/p, h_b<0 left and >0 right (stable for iETS_I; h_a=-h_b gives stable for iETS_O, same root); x*>p iff atanh(1-p)/(1-p)>atanh(p)/p iff p<1/2 (atanh(t)/t increasing); R(1/2)=1 gives x*<1/2 for p<1/2 (mirror for p>1/2). Numerics at 40 digits on 1,999 p plus p=1e-9, 1-1e-9: 0 unreduced identities, 0 counterexamples, root residual <7e-41, one sign change on 2,999 x-points for 80 p. DISPUTE: the claim says 'for every p in (0,1)' the additive root is 'strictly between p and one half'. At p=1/2 the root is exactly 1/2 (AC3.RS10 = 0.5), equal to p, so it is not strictly between; derivations.md and E27 s6 state the exception, the claim statement drops it. Correction: 'strictly between p and one half for p != 1/2, and equal to 1/2 at p = 1/2'. The mathematical content is otherwise confirmed."}}
{"seq":29,"id":"AC3.CK3","type":"check","at":"2026-10-30T14:09:25Z","by":"AC3","prev":"sha256:335129a97136d64f29dcac752ef510e4a967403dc45a1bf1eeef17cc832d6428","content_hash":"sha256:509a959dfd7030a59f225bbde4d842dc50883ccca709eb2daa79b144834209f3","supersedes":null,"origin":null,"body":{"target":"H7","outcome":"confirmed","extent":"full","notes":"AC3.RN3 (results AC3.RS13-RS16; own code). Sympy: with mu=exp(m), p_O=mu/(1+mu), p_I=1/(1+mu), d/dm of o log p+(1-o)log(1-p) equals o-p_O and p_I-o; dp/dlog mu = +-p(1-p). E[o-x]=p-x, E[x-o]=x-p, so the zero is x=p only (linear) and the drift sign moves p_hat towards p for both models (iETS_O: x<p raises mu_a and p; iETS_I: x<p lowers mu_b and raises p); checked on grid with no failures. Positivity: 1+alpha*e equals (1-alpha)+alpha(1-x) (iETS_O,o=0), 1+alpha(1-x) (O,o=1), 1+alpha x (I,o=0), (1-alpha)+alpha x (I,o=1), all >0 for alpha in (0,1], x in (0,1) (sympy identity, analytic; also 50x999 grid, 0 failures); fails for alpha>1 (e.g. alpha=1.1,x=0.95). 0 unreduced identities, 0 counterexamples. Caveat only: in double precision p_hat=mu/(1+mu) rounds to exactly 1.0 for mu>~1e17 and then alpha=1,o=0 gives state 0 (AC3.RS13), a rounding artefact, not a failure of the formal statement."}}
{"seq":30,"id":"AC3.CK4","type":"check","at":"2026-10-30T14:09:28Z","by":"AC3","prev":"sha256:51e2bf00a5927ce422297fc320f998f20c7978511ea0db2c8971d6d84653be37","content_hash":"sha256:f4ca8dd2eaad81f88741d5b7db5332f5ded8aad6f31196c969c3e4b834eb1e6b","supersedes":null,"origin":null,"body":{"target":"H13","outcome":"confirmed","extent":"full","notes":"AC3.RN4 (results AC3.RS17-RS22; own code). (1) D16: log mu_t = log mu_{t-1}+alpha log(1+e), so the filter is additive with error log(1+e); for the old proxy log(1+e)=log(u/(1-u)) (resp. reciprocal) is the additive old error, hence identical drift and zero-drift point. (2) Multiplicative score proxy 1+e=1+s: iETS_O k_O(x)=p log(2-x)+(1-p)log(1-x), k_O'=-p/(2-x)-(1-p)/(1-x)<0, k_O(0+)=p log2>0, k_O(1-)=-inf, so unique root; k_O(p)<0 strictly (log y<y-1, E[s]=0, s non-degenerate), so root<p; stable (positive left, negative right, mu_a up raises p). iETS_I k_I=p log x+(1-p)log(1+x), k_I'>0, k_I(0+)=-inf, k_I(1-)=(1-p)log2>0, k_I(p)<0, so unique root >p; stable. Sympy identities and limits agree. At 40 digits for 1,999 p plus p=1e-9,1-1e-9: roots found with root<p (O) and root>p (I), smallest gaps 3.07e-10 (at p=1e-9, still positive), stability and single sign change (80 p) confirmed; e.g. iETS_O root at p=0.5 is 0.38197. (3) Exponential score: log(1+e)=s, drift +-(p-x), zero-drift point p. 0 unreduced identities, 0 counterexamples (AC3.RS17, RS18). The claim's text is accurate; the old-proxy statement is true by definition (tautological once D16 is applied)."}}
